BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOOK READING: THE SUN WILL SHINE ON MY TOMORROW\, BY SANDEE MACGRE
 GOR
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T203000
UID:bm-6639820261030@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/THE_SUN_W
 ILL_SHINE_ON_MY_TOMORROW.jpg?cb=1792681166
DESCRIPTION:📚☀️🌅The book "The Sun Will Shine on My Tomorrow\,”
  by Sandee MacGregor\, tells the true story of Dorice Lusuli\, a young gir
 l in Nairobi\, Kenya\, who lost both of her parents and was left facing fe
 ar\, grief\, and uncertainty about what would come next. Through the care 
 of her grandmother and the support of a caring village\, Baba Nyumbani\, s
 he found the food\, school fees\, and protection she needed\, along with a
  renewed sense of hope for her future.\nSandee Macgregor is a Canadian aut
 hor based in Southern Ontario. Trained as a teacher\, she is the author of
  two bestselling devotionals as well as two children’s books\, "Lucy's A
 doption Story" and "Can I Take It to Heaven?"\nMeet the author and learn a
 bout Dorice's story of resilience growing up as an orphan and about the or
 ganization that supported every step of the way.\nFree to attend. All are 
 welcome! #ReadDifferently📚
LOCATION:Blackhurst Cultural Centre
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TORONTO BOOK LAUNCH - TWO DAYS IN MAYARO\, BY PAMELA MORDECAI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T160000
UID:bm-6605920261107@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/Two_Days_
 in_Mayaro_.png?cb=1792427147
DESCRIPTION:📚🚀🌴A Different Booklist & Goose Lane Editions are pro
 ud to present celebrated author Pamela Mordecai in conversation with journ
 alist Neil Armstrong for the launch of her new collection of Caribbean dia
 sporic short fiction\, TWO DAYS IN MAYARO!\nJamaican Canadian Pamela Morde
 cai's first short story collection\, PINK ICING received glowing reviews\,
  and her debut novel\, RED JACKET\, was shortlisted for the Rogers Writers
 ’ Trust Fiction Prize. She has published nine collections of poetry and 
 books for children. Weaving old time and contemporary stories\, TWO DAYS I
 N MAYARO\, Pamela's second collection of short fiction\, depicts the strug
 gles\, triumphs\, and humour of diaspora life\, creating a world powered b
 y unforgettable characters in language that sings.\nLook forward to a live
  reading by Pamela and a Q&A. Special guest writer Nalo Hopkinson will in
 troduce the author\, and Neil Armstrong will conduct the interview. See y
 ou there - #ReadDifferently!📚
LOCATION:BLACKHURST CULTURAL CENTRE
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
